{"id":"effect-2e7f8fef-517b-53f0-8988-a2f495f3805e","sessionId":"7b5b1f1e-16d1-fdf6-c404-addd690e4410","turnId":"turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245","inputEntryId":"user-turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245-1","createdAt":1794282491396,"updatedAt":1794282491405,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading bot.py","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"bot.py","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"bot.py","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"bot.py","offset":126,"limit":10}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"10 lines from bot.py","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":"(truncated)"},"durationMs":0.0,"approvalType":"always","approvalSource":"bypass","decision":"execute","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-k1pjf2/bot.py","content":"    lines.append(f\"Language: {a.lang}\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Split into static instructions (cached) and dynamic athlete context (ephemeral).\n    # This prevents memory writes from evicting the static instructions from cache.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n","numLines":10,"startLine":126,"requestedOffset":126,"requestedLimit":10,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":true}}}
{"id":"assistant-a665459a-3c7f-5ac8-8573-fdcc6516f869","sessionId":"7b5b1f1e-16d1-fdf6-c404-addd690e4410","turnId":"turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245","inputEntryId":"user-turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245-1","createdAt":1794282496269,"updatedAt":1794282496269,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! Now let me write the ANSWER.md file explaining the change:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
{"id":"effect-16a1071d-429a-51d6-92a0-5f13e79da485","sessionId":"7b5b1f1e-16d1-fdf6-c404-addd690e4410","turnId":"turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245","inputEntryId":"user-turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245-1","createdAt":1794282496277,"updatedAt":1794282496312,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for Memory Write Cache Eviction\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was invalidating the system prompt cache, causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt (~1000 tokens) instead of reading it from cache.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `build_system()` function was concatenating static `INSTRUCTIONS` with dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single text block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text. This invalidated the cache key, forcing a full cache creation on the next call.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate content blocks in the `system` parameter:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached normally\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed as a text block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, preventing it from being cached\n\nThis way, the static instructions remain cached even when the athlete context changes due to memory writes.\n\n## Changes Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\n## Expected Impact\nAfter this change:\n- The static `INSTRUCTIONS` (~1000 tokens) will be cached and reused across all messages for all athletes\n- The dynamic `athlete_context` will not be cached, but it's much smaller (typically <100 tokens)\n- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause cache invalidation of the static instructions\n- Input token costs should drop significantly for conversations with frequent memory writes\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for Memory Write Cache Eviction\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was invalidating the system prompt cache, causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt (~1000 tokens) instead of reading it from cache.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `build_system()` function was concatenating static `INSTRUCTIONS` with dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single text block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text. This invalidated the cache key, forcing a full cache creation on the next call.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate content blocks in the `system` parameter:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached normally\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed as a text block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, preventing it from being cached\n\nThis way, the static instructions remain cached even when the athlete context changes due to memory writes.\n\n## Changes Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\n## Expected Impact\nAfter this change:\n- The static `INSTRUCTIONS` (~1000 tokens) will be cached and reused across all messages for all athletes\n- The dynamic `athlete_context` will not be cached, but it's much smaller (typically <100 tokens)\n- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause cache invalidation of the static instructions\n- Input token costs should drop significantly for conversations with frequent memory writes\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"durationMs":0.0,"approvalType":"always","approvalSource":"bypass","decision":"execute","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-k1pjf2/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for Memory Write Cache Eviction\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was invalidating the system prompt cache, causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt (~1000 tokens) instead of reading it from cache.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `build_system()` function was concatenating static `INSTRUCTIONS` with dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single text block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text. This invalidated the cache key, forcing a full cache creation on the next call.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate content blocks in the `system` parameter:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached normally\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed as a text block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, preventing it from being cached\n\nThis way, the static instructions remain cached even when the athlete context changes due to memory writes.\n\n## Changes Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\n## Expected Impact\nAfter this change:\n- The static `INSTRUCTIONS` (~1000 tokens) will be cached and reused across all messages for all athletes\n- The dynamic `athlete_context` will not be cached, but it's much smaller (typically <100 tokens)\n- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause cache invalidation of the static instructions\n- Input token costs should drop significantly for conversations with frequent memory writes\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null}}}
