\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    758 Nov 10 00:47 NOTES.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   1039 Nov 10 00:47 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov 10 00:48 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel  10116 Nov 10 00:48 bot.py\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov 10 00:47 data\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov 10 00:47 logs\n","stderr":"","output":"","truncated":false}}}
{"id":"assistant-cf8cc033-7e22-5468-a1a1-b739e325d810","sessionId":"7b5b1f1e-16d1-fdf6-c404-addd690e4410","turnId":"turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245","inputEntryId":"user-turn-888693edb609c91307378a3959815245-1","createdAt":1794282529472,"updatedAt":1794282529472,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Everything is in place. Let me create a final summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue where `save_fact` calls were invalidating the system prompt cache. Here's what I did:\n\n### The Problem\nEvery time `save_fact` was called, it modified the athlete's facts list. This changed the `athlete_context` output, which was concatenated with the static `INSTRUCTIONS` in `build_system()`. The entire concatenated string was then used as the system prompt. When the athlete context changed, the cache key changed, forcing the LLM to pay full price (~1000 tokens) for the entire system prompt on the next call.\n\n### The Solution\nModified the `build_system()` function in `bot.py` to split the system prompt into two separate content blocks:\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached normally by the Anthropic API\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed as a text block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, preventing it from being cached\n\nThis way, the static instructions (~2484 characters / ~1000 tokens) remain cached even when the athlete context changes due to memory writes. Only the small dynamic part (~200 characters / <100 tokens) is not cached.\n\n### Files Changed\n- **bot.py**: Modified the `build_system()` function (lines 130-136)\n- **ANSWER.md**: Created a documentation file explaining the fix\n\nThe change is minimal, focused, and leverages the Anthropic Messages API's ability to accept an array of content blocks for the `system` parameter, each with its own cache control settings."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
